     0→//! Spherical harmonics evaluation for view-dependent color.
     1→//!
     2→//! Gaussians store color as spherical harmonics coefficients rather than
     3→//! a single RGB value. This allows view-dependent effects (specular highlights, etc.)
     4→//!
     5→//! We use degree-3 SH, which requires 16 coefficients per color channel.
     6→
     7→use nalgebra::Vector3;
     8→
     9→/// Evaluate spherical harmonics basis functions up to degree 3 (real SH).
    10→///
    11→/// `direction` must be normalized.
